nd you can do  all the types of plotting all the types  of gating  density plots contour plots histograms  back gating everything you're used to  for primary flow analysis you can do in  fcs express so i'm not going to  focus on that for now i want to show you  some of the  novel features so if i jump to one of  the later pages for example  you can see here is actually a summary  of all of the  a lot of the cell populations within the  given  samples and you can see that  what we have here is comparing our two  different treatments s1 and s2  and the different uh cell subsets and  the percentages between them  and you can see at the top of the page  we actually calculate  in real time a p value showing the  statistical  difference between the s1 and s2  populations  across that um across that particular  gate or across that particular cell type  that we're looking at  these all update in real time as you're  moving your gates around so if i would  go to some of the other pages and move  the gates these would be updated as soon  as i got back  and i wanted to just point out that one  of this is made possible by one of the  really innovative features of fcs  express that being our integrated  spreadsheets  so you can see here that this actually  what i'm clicking in  is a spreadsheet these values in the  spreadsheet are not hard  coded they are actually statistics that  are linked to the various plots and  gates and quadrants  and whatever you're used to and they  update based on those  so these guys here are just statistics  that are pulled in from various places  in the analysis  but if i click in this cell mean s1 you  can see that  you actually can enter excel formulas  and average out the results of all of  these four  populations okay so you can combine  all the excel formulas that you're used  to with live  updating statistics that are updating as  your analysis changes  so this particular analysis for example  has  has  whoops sorry i jumped to the wrong page  you can see in this template that we  have  the average and we have the standard  deviation  formulas that we're calculating from our  samples  but just to show that we actually  support a wide  array all of the formulas that you  expect from excel  you can see a huge list of statistical  formulas  math and trigonometry formulas lookup  and reference formulas date and time  formulas logical formulas so you can do  if then  else so all of the complex analysis that  you  um can do with with excel you can all do  it within fcs express  except you can do it on all of your  primary flow data  all of your gated statistics that are  updating in real time  as you move your gates okay and i can  show that as a quick example i think on  this page  you see here that there's this  eosinophil bar plot and as i move my  eosinophil gate around  you can see that the bars and the bar  plots and the p values  and everything is updating in real time  as i move my gates around  okay so we support a lot of these plots  for pie charts bar  charts statistical regression charts a  lot of different things  again all have the um ability to  combine data from different samples in  novel ways and let you visualize them  um the last thing i wanted to show you  also is a example of how easy it is to  perform high dimensional data analysis  in fcs express  so one of the more common  statistical tools or visualization tools  that are used um  in this days is tisney and i just want  to show you how easy it is to apply a  disney analysis to your data  so you see i clicked here on the  transformation window and i already had  created a disney transformation and i'm  going to select which parameters i want  to participate in my disney  and i've already selected that i want my  disney to be based on cd19 cd4 cd8  cd6 cd45r0 and cd45ra  and so the only thing i actually have to  do to calculate the disney is simply  drag this disney onto my plot  and as with any disney it takes a second  or two to do the calculations so  it's done and now when i switch to  disney x  or tis and versus disney y  then you can see here is my disney plot  that i've generated from my data  and then if i quickly want to see all of  the parameters  we have a special plot and i'm going to  say  you know what i want to see  i want to see my disney plot colored on  these parameters  i can actually very quickly and now it's  got  each plot is colored based on a  different parameter  and if i want to format that data for  example  all of them together and potentially  show  a legend to see what um  what marker it's being is each plot is  using  i'm going to turn on the legend and you  see the plots update in real time to  show  the legend and i'm going to choose to  put the legend on the bottom  and you can see that right away now all  of my plots  quickly have a legend showing which  marker they're colored by  and showing that is the disney plot  colored by that particular marker  in that particular plot  okay so this was a very very brief  introduction  um and i don't want to exceed my time  here  um so i do want to thank the organizers  for letting me present  today um if you do have any questions at  all about what you've seen  please either contact your fluidim  representative or once again  just shoot an email to support  lenovosoftware.com  i'll make that big for you so you can  see it  [Music]  and we'll be glad to answer any  questions  that you have okay  thank you very much  a big thank you to dr novo for that  informative presentation  unfortunately dr nova cannot join us for  live q a today  however sean burke will be answering  questions on behalf of dr novo  welcome sean uh we will now start the q  a portion of the webinar  if you have any questions you'd like to  ask please do so now just click the ask  a question box  located on the far left of your screen  let's get started our first question  is going to be is fcs  express21 part 11 compliant  yeah and uh thanks again for uh having  us here and and hosting the presentation  today i'm happy to take that question  so fcs express does have the ability  to enable 21 part 11 compliant features  in the software  so the version of fcs express that comes  with the fluidim instruments will not  have this enabled  however you can contact our team at  support denovosoftware.com to get more  information about that  and essentially the way that fcs express  handles that is  by adding on a security and logging  functionality  so the security functionality allows  folks to restrict access to various  functions  to particular users and groups of users  as well as allowing electronic signature  type capability  and the other half of that is what we  call logging  which is also referred to as audit  trails and these logging and auto trails  is a system that allows you to track  every  change that you make to every single  layout so if you load data  if you move a text box if you move a  gate all that sort of information is  tracked so when you have these  additional add-ons enabled for the  software  it can help you conform with government  regulations such as 21 cfr part 11.  so again you can contact us at support  the nuvosoftware.com if you have any  questions about that  as a follow-up we can get you some more  information there  great and are more algorithms for high  dimensional data reduction planned  yeah absolutely and i know uh dave  alluded to that  that uh you know many more of these  things are coming down the line  so just in the next few months probably  by the end of the summer we're going to  have  a brand new pipelines tool in fcs  express that's going to allow you  to not just work with tizzy and spade  it's going to allow you to work with  tools like  umap and som some other kind of  familiar ones that are on the market and  it's also going to allow you to  customize these pipelines with down  sampling steps up sampling steps  to hopefully help you come up with new  algorithms on your own without having to  have any sort of programming or r  scripting knowledge  it's all through a pretty easy to use  interface directly in the software  and can i add more users or licenses to  my free one-year license  yeah so the the licenses that are going  to be coming with the flu dime  instruments  are what we call internet dongle  licenses  and essentially what that allows folks  to do is  install the software on as many  computers as they want  and one person at a time can use that  license  it means that you can set up 10 users 20  users 100 on that license but one person  at a time can use it  so you do have a lot of flexibility even  with the license  that comes with the software to put it  on as many computers as you want  however if you do need simultaneous  access you need two  three four people analyzing data at the  same time  we can enable that all you have to do is  contact our team at support  and you know for whatever the cost is we  can add those  additional users to the license and then  you can have a multi-user license at any  time  um so a question here are p values  adjusted for multiple testing  yes i think that that question probably  goes back to  the bar plots and the box and whisker  plots  that dave novo was showing during the  presentation  so uh the way that the p-values work in  fcs express  is just like you would work in a  spreadsheet in microsoft excel  so whatever data that you have in that  spreadsheet  is going to be what the p-values are are  based off of  so in the example that was being shown  it was two sets  of um i believe four tubes  each that were being compared to each  other so if you have multiple sets you  can either use the data list the kind of  move  between them you can add additional sets  of data  so really the way to think about it is  whatever you might do in microsoft excel  whatever you might do  in a tool like prism you can do that  same thing in fcs express you just have  to have the data loaded into the layout  and when you do that not only can you  you know compare  against multiple testings you get that  live  updating of gates or live updating of  statistics  as you move gates and you change data  files around  and why use fcs express with maxpar  if analysis can be done automatically  with path setter  yes i mean there's there's a lot of  advantages to using fcs express  i know from what i've seen past setter  does some really great things i'm sure  it has some you know really great  functionality that you want to use i  mean there's no reason  to not use path setter for for certain  things but where fcs express really  excels  is getting you those results very  quickly and very easily  through you know some of these  predefined templates that we have  we can see the changes that are being  made to the downstream  final results as gates update in real  time which is pretty nice  and also one thing we didn't really put  a lot of focus on just for the interest  of time is that when you're ready to get  those results out  whether it needs to go out to powerpoint  to pdf to high resolution images  fcs express has some very quick and easy  export tools  so if you needed to export some of your  disney plots and some of that  reported information to say powerpoint  you can literally click a button and  that data will be exported in whatever  resolution you want  so imagine you know you're going to a  conference um you know a real conference  one day we'll we'll be able to get back  and do that pretty soon which will be  pretty fun  uh but if you need a 300 dpi image for  your poster  well you can just set that in fcs  express you can hit the export button  and that's what we kind of refer to as a  final result right having that  uh graphic that's up there for your  poster at a presentation having that  graphic  that's ready to be sent off to the  publisher those are the things that fcs  express can  really help you with so again i think  pathsiter is a really great tool i think  fcs express can complement it  in a lot of ways when it comes to the  downstream and  final results that we get out  all right and looks like we're gonna  have time for one more question here  um can gating analysis be automated  or do they need to be adjusted manually  from sample to sample  yeah it's a great question so so right  now there is no um  i guess what we call automatic gating in  fcs  express however we do have uh  and we will be having more of these are  kind of predefined templates for  analysis  so just like dave showed today the the  max par  immune profiling assay template that he  brought up  that sort of template is going to be  able to be downloaded from the de novo  software website it's going to be able  to be downloaded from the fluidim  website  and essentially what will happen there  is you'll have some predefined gating  positions  and you have predefined gates for as  many gates as you want  and when you load the data in all of  that part of it will be done  we won't adjust those gates to you know  say the 90th percentile of data or  something like that  um so you do have to go through and  review gates you know you do have to  make sure  um that the gates are in the correct  positions but when you get them  in the correct positions you know we can  save that in fcs express you can use  that  from sample to sample we also have some  nice functionality in the software where  if you kind of have a a group of data  that all needs to be gated in the same  way  you can save kind of predefined gating  positions so as you move from one group  of data to another  um you know even though it's not being  automatically gated  you know by some sort of artificial  intelligence or something like that  predefined gating positions are allowed  and it should make things pretty  straightforward  for for doing any sort of analysis  awesome well thank you so much son for  your time today and we really appreciate  you being with us  that's no problem and thanks again for  everybody to uh come out and join in the  summit today it's been a lot of fun to  watch the presentations we really  appreciate you coming out today too  it has well before we go i'd like to  thank the audience for joining us today  and for their interesting questions  questions we did not have time for today  and those submitted during the on-demand  period  will be addressed by the speaker via the  contact information you provided  at the time of registration this webcast  can be viewed on demand through july  of 2021 until next time goodbye
 

